<h1 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">What Brennan Uses</h1>

<div class="space-y-8">
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">I prioritize open‑source software where possible and try to choose tools that respect privacy and portability.</p>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Development</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-2">
      <li><strong>Editor:</strong> <a href="https://www.sublimetext.com/4">Sublime Text 4</a></li>
      <li><strong>Terminal:</strong> <a href="https://www.apple.com/macos/">macOS Terminal</a> / <a href="https://iterm2.com/">iTerm2</a></li>
      <li><strong>Browser:</strong> <a href="https://www.mozilla.org/firefox/">Firefox</a> / <a href="https://www.google.com/chrome/">Chrome</a> (DevTools)</li>
      <li><strong>Version Control:</strong> Git + <a href="https://github.com/brennanbrown">GitHub</a>, transitioning over to <a href="https://source.tube/brennan">Source.tube</a> and <a href="https://gitlab.com/brennankbrown">GitLab</a></li>
      <li><strong>Timekeeping:</strong> <a href="https://wakatime.com/">WakaTime</a></li>
      <li><strong>Static Site Generators:</strong> <a href="https://www.11ty.dev/">Eleventy (11ty)</a> (primary), <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a>, <a href="https://gohugo.io/">Hugo</a>, <a href="https://jekyllrb.com/">Jekyll</a></li>
      <li><strong>Comments:</strong> <a href="https://webmention.io/">webmention.io</a> · <strong>POSSE:</strong> <a href="https://brid.gy/">Bridgy</a></li>
      <li><strong>AT Protocol:</strong> Cross-posting to Bluesky via <a href="https://standard.site/">Standard.site</a> and a custom publishing pipeline built on <a href="https://sequoia.rest/">Sequoia</a>, with a Sharp-based image compression workflow</li>
      <li><strong>Styling:</strong> <a href="https://tailwindcss.com/">Tailwind CSS</a> and classless stylesheets like <a href="https://oxal.org/projects/sakura/">Sakura CSS</a> and <a href="https://edwardtufte.github.io/tufte-css/">Tufte CSS</a></li>
      <li><strong>Hosting/Deploy:</strong> <a href="https://www.netlify.com/">Netlify</a> (primary); also <a href="https://www.nearlyfreespeech.net/">NearlyFreeSpeech</a> and <a href="https://www.pikapods.com/">PikaPods</a>; homelab self-hosting for <a href="https://folk.zone">Folk Zone</a></li>
      <li><strong>Transactional Email:</strong> <a href="https://resend.com/">Resend</a></li>
      <li><strong>Domain Management:</strong> <a href="https://www.namecheap.com/">Namecheap</a>, transitioning over to <a href="https://porkbun.com/">Porkbun</a></li>
      <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="https://privateemail.com/">Private Email</a> via Namecheap</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Why: simple, static-first stack that’s fast, accessible, and cheap to run; fits IndieWeb values.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Media</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-2">
      <li><strong><a href="https://libbyapp.com/">Libby</a>:</strong> Digital library app for borrowing e-books and audiobooks</li>
      <li><strong><a href="https://thestorygraph.com/">StoryGraph</a>:</strong> Book tracking and social reading platform</li>
      <li><strong><a href="https://pocketcasts.com/">Pocket Casts</a>:</strong> Podcast listening app—see my <a href="https://brennan.day/podroll/">podroll</a> for recommended shows</li>
      <li><strong><a href="https://www.kanopy.com/">Kanopy</a>:</strong> Streaming service for movies and documentaries</li>
      <li><strong><a href="https://calibre-ebook.com/">Calibre</a>:</strong> E-book management and conversion software</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Learning</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-2">
      <li><strong><a href="https://www.duolingo.com/">Duolingo</a>:</strong> Language (French) and chess learning app</li>
      <li><strong><a href="https://www.clozemaster.com/">Clozemaster</a>:</strong> Language (French) learning app</li>
      <li><strong><a href="https://apps.ankiweb.net/">Anki</a>:</strong> Spaced repetition flashcard system</li>
      <li><strong><a href="https://lichess.org/">Lichess</a>:</strong> Open-source chess platform for games and puzzles</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Writing & Notes</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-2">
      <li><strong>Daily journaling:</strong> <a href="https://750words.com/">750words</a></li>
      <li><strong>Knowledge base:</strong> <a href="https://bear.app/">Bear</a></li>
      <li><strong>Longform writing:</strong> <a href="https://ulysses.app/">Ulysses</a></li>
      <li><strong>Format:</strong> Markdown + YAML/TOML front matter</li>
      <li><strong>CLI Publishing:</strong> <a href="https://writer.brennan.day">writer-cli</a></li>
      <li><strong>Publishing:</strong> <a href="https://blog.brennanbrown.ca/">Medium</a></li>
      <li><strong>Reading:</strong> Kobo Nia eInk reader</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Why: Markdown-first workflow, portable formats, plain text survives. Daily 750-word practice maintains writing discipline. Medium monetization successful.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Design</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-2">
      <li><strong>UI/Assets:</strong> <a href="https://www.figma.com/">Figma</a> / <a href="https://www.canva.com/">Canva</a> / <a href="https://www.rawpixel.com/public-domain">RawPixel Public Domain</a> / <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Main_Page">Wikimedia Commons</a></li>
      <li><strong>Image editing:</strong> <a href="https://www.gimp.org/">GIMP</a>, <a href="https://inkscape.org/">Inkscape</a>, <a href="https://krita.org/">Krita</a>, <a href="https://pixlr.com/e">Pixlr</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Why: fast iteration for assets; more open‑source tools when possible.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Productivity & Ops</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-2">
      <li><strong>Project management:</strong> <a href="https://todoist.com/">Todoist</a></li>
      <li><strong>Scheduling:</strong> <a href="https://calendly.com/brennanbrown/consult">Calendly</a></li>
      <li><strong>CRM:</strong> <a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/crm">HubSpot (free)</a> / <a href="https://capsulecrm.com/">Capsule</a></li>
      <li><strong>Invoicing:</strong> <a href="https://www.waveapps.com/">Wave</a>; Payments via <a href="https://stripe.com/">Stripe</a></li>
      <li><strong>Community:</strong> <a href="https://discord.gg/4qdJecDNkt">Discord</a>; Membership via <a href="https://www.patreon.com/cw/brennankbrown">Patreon</a></li>
      <li><strong>Commitment & focus:</strong> <a href="https://www.beeminder.com/">Beeminder</a> (17 goals fed by Apple Health, Fitbit, StoryGraph, Duolingo, Clozemaster, Lichess, Tumblr/IFTTT, Medium, <a href="https://github.com/brennanbrown/bearminder">Bearminder</a>, GitHub, Todoist, WakaTime, and Bluesky), <a href="https://www.rescuetime.com/">RescueTime</a></li>
      <li><strong>Analytics:</strong> Privacy‑focused first: <a href="https://plausible.io/">Plausible</a>, <a href="https://umami.is/">Umami</a>, <a href="https://neatstats.net/">NeatStats</a>; optionally <a href="https://www.netlify.com/products/analytics/">Netlify Analytics</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Why: lean tools with generous free tiers and client-collab friendly workflows.</p>
  </section>

